<text>
Reason:
<text>

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ipu1_gfclk_mux: ipu1_gfclk_mux@520 {
	...
	clocks = <&dpll_abe_m2x2_ck>, <&dpll_core_h22x2_ck>;
	...
};
```
Reason:
The removal of the `ipu1_gfclk_mux` clock definition during the conversion to a new clock control layout caused the loss of the correct clock source parenting for the IPU1 functional clock. This meant that the IPU1 clock was no longer correctly sourced from `dpll_core_h22x2_ck`, leading to incorrect frequency and operation.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
assigned-clocks = <&ipu1_clkctrl DRA7_IPU1_MMU_IPU1_CLKCTRL 24>;
assigned-clock-parents = <&dpll_core_h22x2_ck>;
```
Reason:
These statements re-establish the correct clock source parenting for the IPU1 functional clock by assigning it to the `dpll_core_h22x2_ck`, ensuring that the IPU1 clock operates at the intended frequency and is independent of the ABE DPLL, thus restoring the previous logic.

